Dockerfile
# `dist` alone only matches the root folder; the glob form is what actually keeps
# locally-built package dist/ out of the image (a bare `dist` once let a stale local
# build ship inside the 0.84 image).
dist
**/dist
docs
**/node_modules
# Local turbo / prewarm leftovers must never enter the build context: `COPY . .`
# would bake a stale piece cache over the one prewarm-pieces.sh builds in-image.
**/.turbo
cache
# NOTE: hermes/ is deliberately NOT ignored — hermes/pieces.json, the scripts and
# hermes/tarballs/*.tgz (in-house pieces, on no public registry) must ship in the
# context for the offline-store bake and piece prewarm layers.
# ...but the e2e fixture manifest is CI-only (it prewarms the versions
# test/integration/ce pins, which are older than the shipped allowlist). It must never
# reach the image: `pieces.json` is the single runtime allowlist, and a second manifest
# in hermes/ invites prewarming the wrong one.
hermes/pieces.e2e-fixtures.json
